 Headings should create chapter rhythm and guide attention. They should not become verbose feature summaries.
 
+Product-detail typography must expose hierarchy through size, weight, tone and spacing together, not size or opacity alone. Use a small set of page-level roles for display, section heading, identity/eyebrow, lead, detail and secondary/scope copy. Preserve legibility over the actual media: photo-backed roles may require denser tones than white-surface roles. Compare headline/lead, local heading/detail and detail/scope in rendered screenshots before accepting the hierarchy.
+
 Responsive visual line breaks must preserve:
 
 - one semantic heading
